this is an okapi  they may look like zebras but they are  actually the only living relative of  giraffes  endemic to the democratic republic of  congo the okapi is a solitary animal  that lives only in dense forests  their coloring is distinctive  their deep red coat contrasts with black  and white markings across their hind  side and legs  these specific markings act as  camouflage among the trees  similar to giraffes okapis have long  tongues that they use to pull leaves  from branches  their tongues are between 14 and 18  inches in length  so long that they can clean their ears  and eyes with it  the okapi are known for having  incredible hearing  their large ears can detect the  slightest disturbance around them which  helps protect them from predators  it is believed that in the last decade  okapi populations have been halved due  to deforestation and hunting  the presence of armed groups in their  native habitat makes conservation  efforts nearly impossible but local  governments are stepping up the okapi is  a fully protected species under  congolese law and is a national symbol  for the country  this is an okapi  [Music]  you
 

